  "body": "@annevk's https://github.com/w3c/ServiceWorker/commit/883fe798a178d5f5a5de653b1be21bb78949d81b used `for=\"environment settings object\"` to reference [the environment settings object's global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-settings-object-global). I was expecting `<a>global object</a>` without `for` attribute goes to https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#global-object, but it raises a bikeshed LINK ERROR: Multiple possible 'dfn' refs for 'global object', and actually goes to `#concept-settings-object-global`.\n",
